{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "04X4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$j : (\\Sch/S)_{fppf} \\to (\\Sch/S')_{fppf}$", "MATH_0002": "$S/S'$", "MATH_0003": "$(\\Sch/S')_{fppf}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{X} = [U/R]$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{X}' = \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{X}' = [U'/R']$", "MATH_0008": "$p$", "MATH_0009": "$U' \\to S$", "MATH_0010": "$R' \\to S$", "MATH_0011": "$\\mathcal{X} = [U'/R']$", "MATH_0012": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-lemma-localize-stacks}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f40449915a277953d7dd920e8dfe627130852e1e692d526dc8d285c3b02cf3b4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:de0c33dde9b51d6eeeaa9e26c62e258d87b64ba63c46091aed6918e78dd83abf", "source_text": "The statement makes sense as the functor\n<MATH_0001>\nis the localization functor associated to the object <MATH_0002>\nof <MATH_0003>. By\nStacks, Lemma <REF_0001>\nthe only thing to show is that the constructions A and B\npreserve the subcategories of algebraic stacks.\nFor example, if <MATH_0004> then construction A\napplied to <MATH_0005> just produces\n<MATH_0006>. Conversely, if <MATH_0007>\nthe morphism <MATH_0008> induces morphisms of algebraic spaces\n<MATH_0009> and <MATH_0010>, and then <MATH_0011>\nbut now viewed as a stack over <MATH_0012>. Hence the lemma is clear.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:55fcf3cc2621f51ffa9cf14bc0c027c3eb8fe1ca7c5b9047d42d21df196d555f", "unit_id": "tag:04X5:proof"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "04X4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Sch_{fppf}$", "MATH_0002": "$S \\to S'$", "MATH_0003": "$p : \\mathcal{X} \\to (\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0006": "$S'$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\mathcal{X} \\longrightarrow (\\Sch/S')_{fppf}\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-category-of-spaces-over-smaller-base-scheme}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-viewed-as}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5a108b4484b44100b6aa01159c0a3eaa99ec65224bd2c91801b419fc384c2ee3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:178fb68fd5ea59197f8b4cd74f7fb2409eaed3721abc4ec6ae77590dd9043a98", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a big fppf site.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a morphism of this site.\nIf <MATH_0003>\nis an algebraic stack over <MATH_0004>, then\n<MATH_0005> <TEXTITOPEN_0001>viewed as an algebraic stack over <MATH_0006><TEXTITCLOSE_0001>\nis the algebraic stack\n<MATH_0007>\ngotten by applying construction A of\nLemma <REF_0001>\nto <MATH_0008>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:fce7de6c59886fc0753d05418e83751e404f1a15c16167c2a608049d906d88c0", "unit_id": "tag:04X6:statement"}
{"chapter": "algebraic", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "04X4", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{X}'$", "MATH_0002": "$S'$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$2$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\mathcal{X}'_S\n=\n(\\Sch/S)_{fppf} \\times_{(\\Sch/S')_{fppf}} \\mathcal{X}'\n$$", "MATH_0006": "$S'$", "MATH_0007": "$1$", "MATH_0008": "$p : \\mathcal{X}'_S \\to (\\Sch/S)_{fppf}$", "MATH_0009": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-2-fibre-product}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-category-of-spaces-over-smaller-base-scheme}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:042f85247db6ba05425fa8fd98122d89f34dc2047fe276e5f9e7b2a07edd461f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e0ee6a39e227b66b8de9ba7f650d54e1f2b363c9aadcd1ffcd4907dbbc1d09e5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nConversely, what if we start with an algebraic stack <MATH_0001>\nover <MATH_0002> and we want to get an algebraic stack over <MATH_0003>?\nWell, then we consider the <MATH_0004>-fibre product\n<MATH_0005>\nwhich is an algebraic stack over <MATH_0006> according to\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nMoreover, it comes equipped with a natural <MATH_0007>-morphism\n<MATH_0008> and hence by\nLemma <REF_0002>\nit corresponds in a canonical way to an algebraic stack over <MATH_0009>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:36a76e8b95ebe4605e54b45ac25d0ade7280488279a0fc7d7b7b8ecc09ce23a1", "unit_id": "tag:04X4:prose-0002"}
